cabal-version:   3.0
name:            agent-workflows
version:         0.1.0.0
synopsis:        John's commands, agents and skills as priced agent-cat programs
description:
  This package is a __user of agent-cat__, not part of it. agent-cat is the
  language — @Agentic.Workflow@'s authoring surface, its Lean kernel, its frozen
  corpus and its conformance gates — and it is public. This is the toolbox: the
  commands, agents and skills under @~\/src\/nix\/config\/ai@ rewritten as
  programs that can be /priced before they are run/.
  .
  The library is @Workflows.*@ and it is layered. @Workflows.Prose@ and
  @Workflows.Prelude@ are the mechanics an author imports.
  @Workflows.Parties@ says who answers and @Workflows.Evidence@ says with what —
  every argv in the tree is in that one module, and it is reviewable as a unit.
  @Workflows.Rubrics.*@ is the corpus's prose, one binding each, every binding
  naming the file and section it was transcribed from. @Workflows.Panels@,
  @Workflows.Deciders@, @Workflows.Gates@, @Workflows.Escalation@ and
  @Workflows.Report@ are the shapes the programs are built out of. The programs
  themselves are thin over that library, by design: if a flagship is long, the
  library is wrong.
  .
  @Workflows.Registry@ is the index and @wf@ is @Agentic.Cli.cliMain registry@ —
  two lines, which is the point of the @Agentic.Cli@ extraction. It is a
  __second__ registry beside agent-cat's examples, because the two are held to
  two different gates: @ci\/examples.sh@ pins seven numbers by equality, because
  those numbers are evidence about the language; @ci\/workflows.sh@ pins @level@
  and @paths@ by equality and holds @costMax@ as a ceiling that only ratchets
  down, because a lens added to a roster moves every other number and that is a
  Tuesday, not a regression.
  .
  What this tree must never do: never import from agent-cat's @test\/corpus@ or
  @tier1@ (it cannot — the package cannot see them); never write outside the
  directory a run was given; and never point a @running@ party at
  @~\/src\/nix\/config\/ai@, which was read as data and is read-only, absolutely.

build-type:      Simple
license:         MIT
author:          John Wiegley
maintainer:      jwiegley@positron.ai

common settings
  ghc-options:      -Wall
  default-language: Haskell2010

  -- Narrowed to what the tree actually uses. The toolbox writes prompts and
  -- argv lists; it does not parse JSON, walk a filesystem or start a process —
  -- `agentic` does all of that behind `Agentic.Cli`, and a dependency this
  -- package does not name is a dependency it cannot quietly grow a use of.
  build-depends:
    , agentic
    , base
    , text

library
  import:          settings
  hs-source-dirs:  src
  exposed-modules:
    -- the mechanics, and the one import an author writes
    Workflows.Prose
    Workflows.Prelude

    -- who answers, and with what
    Workflows.Parties
    Workflows.Evidence

    -- what the prompts say, transplanted from ~/src/nix/config/ai
    Workflows.Rubrics.Discipline
    Workflows.Rubrics.Fess
    Workflows.Rubrics.Finding
    Workflows.Rubrics.Ladder
    Workflows.Rubrics.Personas
    Workflows.Rubrics.Reviewers
    Workflows.Rubrics.Stances
    Workflows.Rubrics.Voice

    -- the shapes
    Workflows.Deciders
    Workflows.Escalation
    Workflows.Gates
    Workflows.Panels
    Workflows.Report

    -- the programs, and the index
    Workflows.Account
    Workflows.Fess
    Workflows.DiscoverBundles
    Workflows.ProcessChecklist
    Workflows.ClaudeMd
    Workflows.CommentAudit
    Workflows.Confer
    Workflows.EliminateDeadCode
    Workflows.DenotationalDesign
    Workflows.WiggumDuet
    Workflows.Effort
    Workflows.ExpenseReport
    Workflows.Fix.Green
    Workflows.Git.Commit
    Workflows.Git.Stack
    Workflows.Hello
    Workflows.Issue
    Workflows.Nix
    Workflows.NodeRed
    Workflows.MeetingNotes
    Workflows.OrgTasks
    Workflows.Partner
    Workflows.PrdArchitect
    Workflows.Productize
    Workflows.Prose.Polish
    Workflows.Qanda
    Workflows.QueryBuilder
    Workflows.Registry
    Workflows.Retest
    Workflows.Review.Ladder
    Workflows.Service
    Workflows.Teams
    Workflows.Threads
    Workflows.TranscribeImage
    Workflows.Translate
    Workflows.TronDebug
    Workflows.Wiggum

-- The owner's entry point. Two lines over `Agentic.Cli`, which agent-cat's
-- `agentic-run` is also two lines over: one CLI, two registries.
--
-- `-threaded` for the reason `agentic-run` takes it: a `wf run … --engine acp`
-- turn's budget is `System.Timeout.timeout` around a request blocked reading the
-- adapter's pipe, and a read is interruptible by an asynchronous exception only
-- under the threaded runtime.
--
-- Install it rather than aliasing `cabal run`: every `running` party's argv
-- executes in the process's working directory, so a wrapper that `cd`s into this
-- package to build would answer `git diff` about the wrong repository.
--
--     cabal install exe:wf --installdir=$HOME/.local/bin --overwrite-policy=always
executable wf
  import:          settings
  hs-source-dirs:  bin
  main-is:         Main.hs
  build-depends:   agent-workflows

  ghc-options:     -threaded
